Understanding Smart Inventories

Smart Inventories are dynamic inventory sources that automatically populate based on defined criteria or filters. Unlike static inventories where you manually define hosts, smart inventories use host facts, variables, and other attributes to dynamically include or exclude systems.
Key Benefits:

• Dynamic Host Selection: Automatically include hosts based on current system state • Reduced Maintenance: No manual inventory updates when systems change • Flexible Targeting: Create multiple views of the same infrastructure • Scalability: Handle large, changing environments efficiently
