Subtask 1.3: Gather Host Facts

Before creating smart inventories, we need to collect facts from all managed hosts.

    Navigate to Resources → Templates

    Create a new Job Template with the following settings:
        Name: Gather Facts Template
        Job Type: Run
        Inventory: Lab Inventory
        Project: Demo Project (or create a new one)
        Playbook: Create a fact-gathering playbook

    Create the fact-gathering playbook:

---
- name: Gather and Display Host Facts
  hosts: all
  gather_facts: yes
  tasks:
    - name: Display OS information
      debug:
        msg: |
          Hostname: {{ inventory_hostname }}
          OS Family: {{ ansible_os_family }}
          OS Distribution: {{ ansible_distribution }}
          OS Version: {{ ansible_distribution_version }}
          Architecture: {{ ansible_architecture }}
          Memory: {{ ansible_memtotal_mb }}MB
          
    - name: Set custom facts for smart inventory filtering
      set_fact:
        server_role: "{{ 'web' if 'web' in inventory_hostname else 'database' if 'db' in inventory_hostname else 'general' }}"
        environment_type: "{{ 'production' if 'prod' in inventory_hostname else 'development' if 'dev' in inventory_hostname else 'testing' }}"
        
    - name: Save custom facts
      copy:
        content: |
          server_role: {{ server_role }}
          environment_type: {{ environment_type }}
        dest: /tmp/custom_facts.yml

    Run the job template to gather facts from all hosts

