Best Practices for Smart Inventories
Performance Optimization

    Efficient Filters: Use specific filters to reduce processing time
    Fact Caching: Enable fact caching to improve sync performance
    Sync Scheduling: Schedule syncs during low-usage periods
    Filter Complexity: Balance filter sophistication with performance

Maintenance Guidelines

    Regular Review: Periodically review and update filter criteria
    Documentation: Document filter logic and intended use cases
    Testing: Test filters in development before production use
    Monitoring: Monitor sync success rates and performance metrics

Security Considerations

    Access Control: Limit smart inventory access to authorized users
    Sensitive Data: Avoid exposing sensitive information in filters
    Audit Trail: Monitor smart inventory usage and changes
    Least Privilege: Grant minimum necessary permissions

Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Hosts Not Appearing in Smart Inventory

Symptoms: Expected hosts don't appear in smart inventory

Solutions:

    Verify host facts are gathered and current
    Check filter syntax for typos or logical errors
    Ensure custom facts are properly formatted
    Test filter components individually

Issue 2: Smart Inventory Sync Failures

Symptoms: Smart inventory sync jobs fail or timeout

Solutions:

    Check system resources and performance
    Simplify complex filters
    Verify database connectivity
    Review error logs for specific issues

Issue 3: Unexpected Host Inclusion/Exclusion

Symptoms: Hosts appear in wrong smart inventories

Solutions:

    Use debug playbook to verify host characteristics
    Review filter logic and operator precedence
    Check for conflicting or overlapping filters
    Validate custom fact values

